---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConceptDepthLinks from '../components/ConceptDepthLinks.astro';
import { sectionMeta, sitePath } from '../data/navigation';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Agentic Engineering Field Guide"
  description="A practical field guide for trustworthy Agentic Engineering: human judgment, AI execution, architecture, context, governance, verification, and iterative learning."
  section="home"
  keywords={['Agentic Engineering','AI agents','AI software engineering','human AI collaboration','agent governance','AI verification']}
>
  <main id="main-content" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="home-hero">
      <div class="shell hero-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Human–AI engineering for trustworthy outcomes</p>
          <h1>Engineer the system, not just the prompt.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Agentic Engineering combines AI speed with the professional engineering practices that make complex work reliable. The model matters—but so do architecture, context, tools, authority, evidence, and human judgment.</p>
          <p><a class="deep-link" href={sitePath('/start/01-elevator.html')}><strong>Start with the 60-second mental model →</strong></a></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="Core principle">
          <span class="pill gold">Core principle</span>
          <h2>AI changes the scale of engineering—not the need for engineering discipline.</h2>
          <p>Agents can multiply useful work dramatically. They can also multiply defects, weak decisions, and low-quality output just as quickly.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="paths">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div><p class="kicker">Choose your learning path</p><h2 id="paths">One system. Four depths.</h2></div>
          <p>Never make someone understand the whole architecture before they can understand the value. Start with the smallest useful mental model and expose the next layer when the next question appears.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="path-grid">
          {(['start','explore','deep','practice'] as const).map((id, index) => (
            <a class="path-card" href={sitePath(sectionMeta[id].landing)}>
              <small>{String(index + 1).padStart(2,'0')}</small>
              <h3>{sectionMeta[id].label}</h3>
              <p>{sectionMeta[id].description}</p>
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="loop">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div><p class="kicker">The operating loop</p><h2 id="loop">The Agentic Engineering Loop</h2></div>
          <p>Human-owned intent moves through architecture-aware Planning and bounded Execution to independent Validation. The system can do substantial work, but consequential judgment remains governed and explicit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow" aria-label="Agentic Engineering operating loop">
          <div class="step">
            <span class="pill gold">Human Owner</span>
            <h3>Sets intent</h3>
            <p class="muted">Provides context and retains consequential judgment, authority, and accountability.</p>
            <ConceptDepthLinks concept="human-owner" />
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <span class="pill gold">Contract</span>
            <h3>Defines success</h3>
            <p class="muted">Goal · Spec · Proof</p>
            <ConceptDepthLinks concept="contract" />
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <span class="pill purple">Planning</span>
            <h3>Designs the route</h3>
            <p class="muted">Plans against the real architecture, constraints, dependencies, and required evidence.</p>
            <ConceptDepthLinks concept="planning" />
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <span class="pill teal">Execution</span>
            <h3>Performs bounded work</h3>
            <p class="muted">Agents use tools, observe, retry, and adapt inside governed boundaries.</p>
            <ConceptDepthLinks concept="execution" />
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <span class="pill green">Validation</span>
            <h3>Determines whether it worked</h3>
            <p class="muted">Independent judgment evaluates evidence against the approved Proof.</p>
            <ConceptDepthLinks concept="validation" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="quote">The system does the heavy lifting, but it does not self-approve.</div>
        <p><a class="deep-link" href={sitePath('/start/03-bridge.html')}><strong>Start Here:</strong> walk through the Agentic Engineering Loop →</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="collaboration">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Human–AI collaboration</p><h2 id="collaboration">Different strengths. Shared work.</h2></div></div>
        <div class="grid two">
          <article class="card blue-line"><span class="pill blue">AI Value</span><h3>Speed, scale, synthesis, and execution</h3><p class="muted">Rapid analysis, broad technical knowledge, persistence, tool use, testing, comparison, and large amounts of bounded execution inside strong engineering rails.</p></article>
          <article class="card gold-line"><span class="pill gold">Human Value</span><h3>Context, logic, ingenuity, creativity, and judgment</h3><p class="muted">Contextual knowledge, taste, values, authority, accountability, and the ability to decide what should happen—not merely what can happen.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="quote"><strong>Target experience:</strong> closer to two colleagues reasoning together at a whiteboard than a human filling out forms for an automation engine.</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="rails">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">The engineering rails</p><h2 id="rails">Speed without compounding errors.</h2></div><p>Agentic Engineering builds on decades of product, software, architecture, security, testing, risk management, and iterative delivery practice.</p></div>
        <div class="grid four">
          <div class="card"><h3>Stable intent</h3><p class="muted">Approved Contract targets do not drift with implementation convenience.</p><ConceptDepthLinks concept="contract" /></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Architecture-aware planning</h3><p class="muted">Work is decomposed against the actual system, decisions, interfaces, and dependencies.</p><ConceptDepthLinks concept="planning" /></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Governed execution</h3><p class="muted">Agents adapt locally without quietly gaining new authority.</p><ConceptDepthLinks concept="execution" /></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Independent evidence</h3><p class="muted">The doer does not control the judge or rewrite Proof.</p><ConceptDepthLinks concept="validation" /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
